# A mutually recursive group whose functions do not agree about what
# they take.
#
# Merging a group gives its functions one accumulator between them, so
# the first slot here would have to be an Int for `ping` and a String
# for `pong` at the same time -- and Pyking has no type that is both in
# a way `+` and `==` could use. The pass merges the group anyway, on
# the syntax alone: how many parameters each takes is something it can
# see, and what type each holds is not.
#
# So the checker refuses what the pass built. This is the one case where
# `--no-tail-call-opt` is not a matter of taste: with the pass off, this
# program is perfectly good, which is what its `.notail.ast.out` shows.
# See docs/optimization.md, "The groups this cannot make work".
#
# This program is expected to FAIL type checking with the pass on. Its
# `.ast.out` holds the error message.

def ping(n: Int) -> String:
    if n == 0:
        "done"
    else:
        pong("x")


def pong(mark: String) -> String:
    if mark == "":
        "empty"
    else:
        ping(0)


print(ping(2))
